WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.589
With only a couple of months to go until the
film's release, Disney tantalized Star Wars

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:09.660
fans with a new trailer for the latest chapter
in the Skywalker saga — Star Wars: The Last

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.660
Jedi.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.700
According to director Rian Johnson, fans who
want to go in completely clean might actually

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.510
want to skip watching the trailer.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:20.500
But if potential spoilers hold no power over
you, let's take a look at what you might've

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.150
missed in The Last Jedi's new trailer.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.349
Luke's biggest fear

00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:28.519
The trailer picks up where The Force Awakens
left off — on the planet Ahch-To, as Rey

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:32.290
hands Luke the lightsaber that was once wielded
by his father, Darth Vader.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:36.739
We then see Rey training with the weapon as
Luke looks on, and it soon becomes clear just

00:00:36.739 --> 00:00:38.680
how innately talented she is.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:43.020
Skywalker looks positively shocked as the
ground cracks open while Rey meditates, and

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:46.870
it's clear he's having flashbacks to what
happened with his last protégé — his nephew

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.770
Ben Solo, who now serves Supreme Leader Snoke
under the name Kylo Ren.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:53.910
"I've seen this raw strength only once before."

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:57.899
It's then that Luke reveals he's actually
afraid of Rey's talents, just as we get a

00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:02.280
more detailed look at the aftermath of the
attack on Luke's Jedi Temple by Kylo and the

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.280
Knights of Ren.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.930
He's clearly reluctant to train her, lest
she turn to the dark side.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.510
Rey's journey

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:12.570
While it's clear that Rey spends some time
with Luke on Ahch-To, she's not going to always

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.100
be on the water's edge.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.080
She's also shown approaching what looks like
a burned tree trunk in a rocky landscape,

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:21.760
and looking down at a book inside Luke's Force-sensitive
treehouse.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.140
In the previous teaser, she was browsing what
many believe is the fabled Journal of the

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.890
Whills, which means Rey is about to get a
lesson in the origins of the Force and the

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.610
Jedi Order from her new teacher.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:35.680
Later, we see a drenched Luke looking up and
saying, "this is not going to go the way you

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:36.680
think."

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.940
Considering we also see Rey diving under the
water near what looks like a fanged sea monster,

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:45.360
it might go exactly like we think it will
— that shot directly aligns with rumors

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.250
that the native Porgs of Ahch-To will demand
that Rey slay a fearsome sea monster in order

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.740
to stay on the planet.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.640
Kylo's moment of truth

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.710
You may have noticed the space battle shots
featuring a new version of the classic TIE

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:58.710
fighter.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:02.090
This is Kylo Ren's personal craft, and it's
called the TIE Silencer.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:06.620
It's supposed to be sort of like the original
trilogy's TIE interceptor and comes equipped

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.670
with laser cannons and missile launchers.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:13.480
In this battle sequence, it appears that Kylo
Ren is setting his sights on a Mon Calamari

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.480
star cruiser.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.420
And since General Leia Organa is shown sitting
down on the bridge, the implication of the

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.900
cutaways between Leia's face and her son's
are clear: each knows the other is there,

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:27.530
and Ben has the opportunity to deal a gigantic
blow to the Resistance by destroying the ship

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:29.560
and — ending the life of his mother.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:33.120
Now for the big question — will he or won't
he pull the trigger?

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.120
Finn's weapon

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:38.500
In one major spoiler given away by the trailer,
we see that Finn has clearly recovered from

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:43.400
the wounds he sustained during The Force Awakens,
and is back in fighting shape for a duel against

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.540
Captain Phasma.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:48.960
Phasma wields a Force pike, while Finn is
carrying a riot-control baton much like the

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.650
one previously carried by the stormtrooper
he fought during the battle on Takodana in

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:54.940
The Force Awakens.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.140
"Traitor!"

00:02:56.290 --> 00:03:00.540
We also couldn't help but notice Finn's First
Order officer's uniform in the following scene

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.990
as he walks somewhere, escorted by stormtroopers.

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:07.510
In case you missed it, he and new character
Rose don those uniforms in behind-the-scenes

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.400
footage that's made its way online.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.290
So since the background behind Finn and Phasma
in their duel looks a lot like the destroyed

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:18.240
remnants of the First Order, this duel might
possibly take place after an secret infiltration

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.000
and sabotage mission by Finn and Rose.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.000
New creatures

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.400
In addition to the previously mentioned Porgs,
The Last Jedi is set to introduce a whole

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.230
bunch of new additions to the Star Wars universe.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:34.190
While we didn't see them in the trailer, Entertainment
Weekly broke the news in August 2017 that

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:39.380
Ahch-To's residents include a group of nun-like
creatures known only as the Caretakers.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:44.209
But the trailer did feature one exciting shot
of another new species: the crystalline fox-like

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:47.490
animals which reside on the mineral world
of Crait.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:48.880
The Battle of Crait

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:52.650
It seems clear from the new trailer — and
all of the other footage released thus far

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:56.350
— that the land-battle on Crait will play
a major role in The Last Jedi.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:04:00.320
The new trailer gives us our first good look
at the massive firepower that the First Order

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:04.340
will bring to bear against the Resistance
on the surface of the planet.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:09.830
Those In place of the regular old Imperial
walkers are the new and improved AT-M6 walkers.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:14.290
One can only hope that these machines are
just as susceptible to proton bombs, harpoons,

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:19.269
and tow cables as their older cousins — or
the Resistance may really be in some trouble.

00:04:19.269 --> 00:04:20.620
Snoke's identity

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:25.690
The trailer doesn't actually give away Snoke's
identity — but it does reveal a big clue.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:29.870
Leading up to the final moments of the trailer,
we hear Snoke apparently telling Rey she needs

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:34.090
to "fulfill your destiny," and it looks like
he's using his powers to torture her.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:37.550
This could also mean that Snoke's voiceover
from the beginning of the trailer where he

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:42.400
talks about someone's "raw untamed power"
could be directed at Rey — and not Kylo

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.400
Ren.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.360
"Let the past die."

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:49.500
Instead of a 30-foot-tall hologram like in
The Force Awakens, this is Snoke in the flesh

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.610
— and his flesh appears to be distinctly
humanoid.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:57.800
That seems to blow the "Snoke is Darth Plagueis"
theory out of the water, since he was an alien,

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:02.169
and it also apparently debunks the "Snoke
is Grand Moff Tarkin" theory, since Snoke

00:05:02.169 --> 00:05:05.350
seems able to use the Force, while Tarkin
couldn't.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:09.690
As for how he got ahold of Rey to begin with,
well, consider the rumors that Kylo will attack

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:14.669
Luke and Rey on Ahch-To, and it seems possible
that Kylo ends up abducting Rey from the planet

00:05:14.669 --> 00:05:16.960
and taking her back to his master.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.840
The Millennium Falcon soars again

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:23.150
In a couple of short clips from the new The
Last Jedi trailer, we see the Millennium Falcon

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:27.630
back in action, diving and twisting through
what appears to be an underground labyrinth.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:32.130
Based on the red crystals we can see, it seems
likely that this dogfight happens in a cave

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.480
somewhere on Crait.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:37.190
And notice how the Porg and Chewbacca are
shown together on the ship, but we don't see

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.560
who's in the pilot seat?

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:43.080
If Kylo abducts Rey, this could spur Luke
— who's not such a bad pilot himself — to

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:47.590
join Chewie and return to his sister Leia
to help her take on the First Order.

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:48.840
Poe's fire

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:53.110
In our first glimpse of Poe Dameron from the
trailer, he's aboard what appears to be some

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:57.790
sort of Mon Calamari lifeboat, which could
point to the starcruiser we saw previously

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.669
getting hit, and promises to:

00:05:59.669 --> 00:06:02.020
"Burn the First Order down."

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:06.139
He hops in his X-Wing — which appears to
have been retrofitted with some sort of afterburner

00:06:06.139 --> 00:06:10.790
— as he dives and spins in an attack run
on the First Order Dreadnought looming above

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:11.790
Crait.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:12.790
Frenemies

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:17.229
Last but not least, there's that seemingly...friendly
exchange between Rey and Kylo.

00:06:17.229 --> 00:06:21.229
This may be some editing misdirection, but
it sure looks like Rey is telling Kylo she

00:06:21.229 --> 00:06:22.300
needs some advice.

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:25.770
This clip of Rey could come from when she
tries to persuade Luke to train her.

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:29.950
But the clip of Kylo Ren is more elusive — he
has his scar, so it can't be a flashback to

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.610
when he destroyed Luke's temple.

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:35.270
Additionally, he's no longer wearing the bandage
we've seen in earlier clips.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:38.479
This could suggest that the clip comes from
near the end of the movie.

00:06:38.479 --> 00:06:40.570
But who could Kylo be extending his hand to?

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:44.790
It's a clip that neatly echoes the visuals
of the scene between Han and his son.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:49.030
So could Kylo be possibly accepting redemption
from the hands of his mother — or his uncle?

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:52.020
Or is it another double cross?

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:57.360
Thankfully, we won't have to wait much longer
to find out.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:58.740
Thanks for watching!

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.479
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:01.479 --> 00:07:03.979
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

